                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.34671/2611.34671v1/method.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:DemoFoundry pipeline.(a) A pair-construction agent writes and refines reconstruction, alignment, and simulation programs to convert diverse existing demonstrations into real–proxy video pairs. (b) The paired dataset supervises a video renderer conditioned on a proxy video and an initial RGB reference frame. (c) In a new scene, an agent builds a task program and executes it under randomized simulator layouts. For successful executions, initial proxy frames guide matching RGB-reference generation before video rendering. Simulation retains actions and robot states for robot learning without new target-task demonstrations.",
